\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Conceptual schematic of the eclipse-modulated SRP work asymmetry in the reduced mechanism picture. For an inertially fixed sail, solar radiation pressure contributes positive work over part of the illuminated orbit and negative work over another part. If eclipse removes a larger fraction of the unfavourable arc than of the favourable arc, the one-orbit SRP work integral becomes positive. The figure is intended to illustrate the phase-selective gating mechanism, not to represent the full propagated 3D geometry directly.}}{3}{figure.caption.1}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{fig:placeholder}{{1}{3}{Conceptual schematic of the eclipse-modulated SRP work asymmetry in the reduced mechanism picture. For an inertially fixed sail, solar radiation pressure contributes positive work over part of the illuminated orbit and negative work over another part. If eclipse removes a larger fraction of the unfavourable arc than of the favourable arc, the one-orbit SRP work integral becomes positive. The figure is intended to illustrate the phase-selective gating mechanism, not to represent the full propagated 3D geometry directly}{figure.caption.1}{}}
